WEBVTT

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.000
She's here!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.870
Pikari!

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.840
Wait up! Pikari!

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.510
Amanchu House

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.480
I win!

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.400
Huh? Were we racing?

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.050
I thought of it this morning.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.900
I figured I could probably beat you if I started running when you came out of the woods.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.450
Maybe next time I'll wait until you reach the bus stop.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.040
You're a real pro when it comes to thinking up fun ideas.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.430
Thanks!

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:11.030
I think that's the most important thing if I want to become an instructor.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.230
That's so cool!

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.910
Please, you'll make me blush!

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.340
You have my full support!

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.110
I couldn't ask for more!

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:07.740
When everything around me was new, and I was surrounded by darkness and anxiety, she was like a shining ray.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.580
She illuminated all the fun things that lay in wait ahead.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.170
That kind of light. {## I wish I knew how to fix this}

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:21.090
In a new town and at a new school, 
Pikari showed me all sorts of new things.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:28.180
And though I had always been scared and frozen in place by the unknown, {## 3. I tried it anyway}

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:38.530
Pikari came to me and brought me happiness, joy, fun, and love. {## 2. if I (or you, for that matter) had the time I'd have this reworked entirely. As I'm sure you know the Japanese has a massive descriptive nominal at the beginning that describes Teko only; the English here instead sets it up as a descriptor for the (unrelated) instance of her meeting Hikari. Fine because it's unwieldy in English (and it's actually forbidden to use adjectivals to modify first or second person pronouns outside of a few exceptions like 'lucky me' or '-self') but it means that this sentence doesn't make sense with the former. Pikari showed her new things, she was spooked by those new things, and then Pikari shows up a -second time-? It's minor enough that I'll gloss over it under the circumstances, but just so you know}

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:48.720
So now, even when faced with a brand-new world, 
I'm confident I can take the first step if I'm with her.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:56.180
My heart was filled to the brim with Pikari before I even noticed.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:01.050
That's why I didn't want to acknowledge

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.000
that eventually, that day would come. {## past tense earlier enforces 'would'}

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:20.110
The shrimp and that eel were so adorable!

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:23.740
Cleaner shrimp do that to remove parasites from the eels.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.260
How lovely!

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.540
The sea is full of lovely things.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.920
Lovely, lovely!

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:32.080
You lovelies are saying "lovely" too much!

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.550
Now then, I think it's pork soup time.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.250
Even in the summer, you can't go diving without pork soup afterwards!

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.450
You said it!

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:41.690
I can't wait!

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.120
Makoto! After you finish changing, 
ask Grandma to pour us some pork soup. {the rest of them will say Grandma, Pikari will say Granny}{## are you dividing entirely on character or on the actual honorific used? / wait, saki ni?}

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.010
All right, got it.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:53.600
Pork soup! Pork soup! Pork— {## I want so badly the rhythmic match of 'pork bone soup' but they're different things}

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:04.870
Three orders of ramen! Plus two Chu-Hi and a Coke. {## alt. generic 'cola', 'Pepsi'. Specifying Chu-Hi and then having generic soda (which Chu-Hi -is-) is inadmissible}

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.910
Coming right up!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.580
What...

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.160
A full house?!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.120
Three extra-large yakisoba, up!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.890
Coming! {## did he finish changing -that much- faster? how did this happen?}{he's male}

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.730
Guys, help us out!

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:16.580
Right!

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:21.050
Just to confirm, that's a fried rice, ramen, and...

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.270
Two curry rice orders ready! {## alt. 'orders' instead of 'servings' / yes, 'rices'}

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.440
Over here!

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.090
Upyo! {## but why tho, and why not in the other like five instances}

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.760
Three more extra-large yakisoba!

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.140
Um... huh?

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:32.280
Ah, excuse me!

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.500
Oh, yes! {## 'cool literal!'}

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.810
And the ramen was for... ah, yes.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.440
Three draft beer, coming right up!

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.010
Everyone good with pork soup?

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.510
I'm down.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.440
It'll be pork soup to remember.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.900
To remember?

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.730
It's going to be a while until the next time we can all dive together.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.170
I'm moving abroad next week.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.540
I see.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.710
Oh, almost forgot.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.620
Could you take our picture?

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.580
Sure!

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:01.710
Here we go.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.060
Thank you. {## sparing with the exclams, aren't we?}

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.800
Let's dig in!

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.720
Eat your fill, and don't hold back.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.290
It's so hot and delicious!

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:21.270
You can have as much shaved ice as you like, too. {## she isn't buying it (from a store at the moment, anyway) so 'treat' is NG}

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.580
Really?

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:24.790
I'll take it all!

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:25.400
Lucky us.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.920
Does that mean we can have the popsicles too? {technically gori gori kun, doesn't really matter}

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.240
Sure thing!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:34.740
Man, are we lucky or what? I'm counting this as Big Summer Event number ten!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.150
Number ten?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.620
Big event?

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:40.460
I've been counting them since summer vacation started.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.090
And there have already been <i>ten</i>?

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.610
This year's been quite high paced.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:49.930
By the way, meeting Akane-chan and Chizuru-chan was number three,

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.060
and promising to see them again was number nine! {## I saw das Finale instead, though; totally worth it}

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:54.250
Even that's on there?

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.850
Yep! There've been big events left and right.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.790
And they're all thanks to you.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:02.260
I'm glad to hear that.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:08.820
But compared to that, you've given me more big events than I can count.{## 'compared to [ten] ... countless'? 'compared to [that size] ... big'? orig. unclear, and 'up until now' is just not nec.}

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.190
<i>I'm always on the receiving end.</i>

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.780
<i>Will it always be that way?</i>

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:26.790
Oh, and also, I heard that the two of you will be coming to Brushie-kun's shop to dive again. {## if you want 'oh yeah', change the timing so it catches the 'ah'}

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.480
Hm? Yeah, next Saturday.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.330
It's been a while.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:34.930
I'll be there as a sub-instructor again.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.280
Oh, you will?

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.480
Amanchu
House

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.020
It's been a while for you, too.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.590
Yeah, because I can't do it during the school year.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:42.810
Makes sense.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.030
Good luck, Pikari!

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.320
Thanks, I'll do my best!

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:47.820
You wanna come too?

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:50.090
Huh? Me?

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.490
Yeah, come on! Do it!

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.160
It'll be fun!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.840
I...

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:02.510
I was thinking about helping out around here again!

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:03.690
With Granny?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:04.250
Yeah.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:08.310
Today was a lot of fun, and I learned a lot too. {## no one actually says 'educational'}

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.350
Tekochin, that's pretty masochistic.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.870
You should do it, Teko!

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.240
Hear that, Granny?

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:19.140
Yep, we'd be glad to have you.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.410
That's great, Teko! You got the okay!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:23.560
Y-Yeah.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:27.840
Good luck!

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.820
Sure, thanks...

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:37.760
I was so sure that Tekochin would want to come along with us.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.320
How unexpected. {## 'that was' somehow sounds highly recent, like an event that took place seconds ago}

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:42.430
Teko's managed to find her own fun.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:43.750
Don't you feel lonely? {## 'at all' too specifically interrogative}

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.670
N-No, not at all... {## and frees it up for use here, though you could also just have 'not really' as originally or 'in particular' to stretch length}

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.410
That's a good wind.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.810
I'm excited to be working with you toda— {## 'to...' reads as 'in order to''s 'to', not 'today''s 'to', especially since it's ... and not a dash}

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.200
The customers...

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.780
This is our usual speed. {## 'this's' doesn't actually indicate a different pronunciation from 'this is', so it's useless. cf. the clear difference between e.g. 'he is' and 'he's', 'd and 've in all situations, etc}

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.970
Grab yourself a drink.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.690
Shall I do some cleaning?

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:27.640
Yesterday was dead too, so I've already got the place spick-and-span. {## supported by Merriam-Webster, Cambridge, and the etymology; apparently Oxford are savages}

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.220
I see.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.640
<i>There's nothing... to do!</i>

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.050
<i>What now?</i>

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:42.460
<i>If Pikari were here, I'm sure she'd be able to find something fun to do.</i>

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.320
<i>It's going good!</i>

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:05.660
<i>Ane-chan-senpai and the other clients all look like they're having a great time. {## something about 'my senpai'...}</i>

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:11.630
<i>I wonder how Teko's doing right now.</i>

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.990
None of you are getting in the hot spring boats?!

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:20.330
I'll pass.

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:21.470
Sorry, me too.

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:24.700
But it's a steaming-hot bath in the summer...

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.140
Yeah, that's exactly why.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.490
See you!

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:29.560
Have fun.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.960
Those guys just don't get it.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:40.770
They don't appreciate the feeling of having every nook and cranny of their tired bodies healed by the spring after a long dive. {## purely nominal 'sentences'... / 'nook and cranny' when referring to bodies is a little gross, but if you like / did this end up at three lines? I can't tell}

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:44.570
Self-care time is always in season! {I'd honestly go with reward time too}{## 'treat yoself time'}

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:51.290
That bikini top looks weirdly similar to mine... {## a bikini is two items}

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.590
Whew, that was incredible.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.520
I felt twenty years younger.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.520
<i>Uh-oh.</i>

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:01.060
<i>I took it off without thinking! {## I would call 'accidental removal' something like your shirt coming off along with your sweater; Hikari -did- take it off and it was no accident, even if not intentional}</i>

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.310
<i>Fortunately, the old man crew went for the second boat,</i>

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.590
<i>If they do, that's four strikes and I'm out! {## there are four old dudes; I'm more in favour of changing the phrase like this more than just using it for a single event counting as three for fudgey reasons}</i>

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:19.290
<i>I must somehow reclaim my top before I end up flashing someone! {## 'nip slip' is such an awful phrase, ugh i hate it}{it's a great phrase, were you too young for that superb owl?}</i>

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.370
Thank goodness! With this, I'm saved!

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:34.000
Nothing!

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.500
Why doesn't anyone have their phones... {## oh, let's not give up this easily}

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.970
I need to at least text Teko... {because like you noticed, she tried calling}

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:46.890
A missed call? {## 'a call' indicates it's going off at the time}

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:52.600
It's from Pikari. Can't she just come over herself and...

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.360
What?! You still haven't gotten out?!

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.940
Look how overheated you are!

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.610
Hang on, I'll lift you out of there.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.490
Attention divers! {## MY HAIR IS TELLING ME IT'S TONJIRU TIME}

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:14.430
Huh? Tekochin?

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.200
I've brought you pork soup from Amanchu!

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:18.710
Is something u— {## if after 'p' it's just the end of the sentence, and you literally cannot be cut off}

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:23.080
I'll leave it here, so please help yourselves!

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:32.430
We've managed to avoid the worst-case scenario at least.

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:36.250
Geez, you're such a dummy, Bakari.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.710
I'm ashamed.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:41.390
If Tekochin hadn't shown up, 
you'd have flashed the whole lot. {## beach...?}{nuhuh}

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.510
Thanks so much, Teko.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:44.910
It was nothing.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:50.370
But I really am glad you didn't end up flashing anybody.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.230
Me too.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.370
I've got it!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:58.590
A wonderful idea to thank my flash-preventing savior Teko! {## the exact descriptive nominal thing (I need to find out what this is actually called) described in the wall o text above, viable for third person pronouns}

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.030
Eh?!

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.510
Leave your schedule open for tonight!

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:04.980
Um, okay.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.890
And so,

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:12.640
tonight I call to order an event to commemorate Teko!

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:18.770
I call it: the Inaugural Thank You Teko Barbecue Party in Amanchu House! {## correct usage of 'inaugural', i checked}

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:24.070
And it goes without saying that the two of you and Mato-chan-sensei are invited too! {## reasons}

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.530
Barbecue!

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.360
It sounds like fun!

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:31.020
Doesn't it?

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.950
But... are you sure?

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:39.040
I have so much I want to thank you for too.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.780
The same goes for us too, Ane-san.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:45.630
I suppose so. Pikari <i>did</i> show us a fun time diving today.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:52.930
Therefore, I propose we change the plan to a Thank You Everyone Barbecue Party!

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.980
Great idea, Teko!

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:56.830
Really?

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:57.900
We're in!

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:01.530
All right, we'll meet back up at seven tonight.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:02.860
Okay!

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.540
Our parents gave us some food to bring.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:29.720
Thanks for organizing.

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:33.970
Make some grilled rice balls too. {## 'use these to' makes it sound like one part of many, not just the like, whole thing to be cooked}

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:36.110
Yo.

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:39.060
I splurged! {not B, but A}

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:49.070
Ready...

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:50.490
Go!

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.700
Let's eat!

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.300
Me too!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:56.790
So good! {## I hope someday to discover a better translation for that than this, but hope grows faint}

00:14:58.610 --> 00:14:59.940
Keep on eating!

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.500
It's super delicious!

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.880
Dibs on the scallop! {## why does she have cat food and bowls}

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:08.800
I brought some for you as well. {I think you missed the memo of avoiding awkward situations when possible}

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.170
Much obliged.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:11.440
You're welcome.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:12.640
Having fun?

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:19.600
I am. It feels like I've been running around in circles all day, but Pikari made it fun.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:23.280
Hikari was always just spinning her wheels too, you know. {## the relation here in the English is unclear, look it over again if you've the time}

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.730
It was especially bad before she met you, Teko-chan.

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.700
Before she met me?

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.800
Wanna throw a barbecue every week from now on?

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.440
No, I think not.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:36.700
She loses sight of her surroundings whenever she's having fun.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:36.700
You're such a Bakari.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:39.570
So she never managed to make any progress.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:45.670
But with you, she's having so much fun it's propelling her forward. {## this doesn't seem to make sense. she's having extra fun so she's extra not making progress, so aren't things worse after meeting Teko? there's something off here}

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.770
It's the same for me.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:52.650
Pikari! I want some grilled onions!

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.250
Got it! Coming right up!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:57.240
I'll grill them, so both of you get your plates ready.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.080
Thank you!

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.960
The rest of you too! There's plenty more to eat!

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:02.790
Okay!

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.350
Thank you.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.320
Is that all you're taking, Mato-chan-sensei? {## 'all you want' does look like it refers to just that amount on the plate, that is 'Is that all [the shrimp] you want'}{finished implies no more any food}

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:12.290
Worried about me? I'm just making sure to leave plenty of space for the star: the crab!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.170
If only I'd thought of that strategy!

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:17.490
It's crab time.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:18.920
Here we go!

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.700
Nice, finally! {## alt. 'waiting for this'}

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.720
I'm so satisfied.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:31.090
And next is... the grilled rice balls!

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.430
Here, pork soup! {## 'Hoi' if I weren't 100% certain somebody'd remove it}

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:38.920
I don't even want to <i>see</i> any more meat or crab...

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:40.240
Me neither...

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:43.560
It's from Chizuru-chan.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.090
Hello, Chizuru-chan?

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:51.480
Well?

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:54.050
Well, uh... it's meat.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:58.030
Oh, come on. Sound a bit more excited, I'm trying to make you jealous. {## ENVY AND JEALOUSY ARE DIFFERENT THINGS AND MISS ME WITH THAT TEENAGE GIRLS WOULD DEFINITELY MAKE THIS MISTAKE ALL THE TIME I CAN'T STAND IT}

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.800
That pic's from a grilling party we had today.

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.740
Wow, that sounds nice.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:05.920
We actually just had a barbecue party over here too.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.760
A barbecue party?

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:12.020
Yeah. Besides the meat, there was also shrimp, scallops, and crab.

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.880
What?! You're making <i>me</i> jealous now!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.130
Sorry!

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.380
It's fine, I'm over it. Hang on a sec.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:20.860
Hello!

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:23.850
Akane-chan! You're there too?

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:28.200
Yeah, we're having a sleepover tonight with two of our classmates. {## I was originally going to just change 'us' to 'we' for correctness but that was awkward even for me}

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.030
Wow, that sounds like fun.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.110
It seems like you're having fun too. Are you celebrating something?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.810
Well, nothing in particular, I guess.

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.430
I see. Is Pikari-chan there too?

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:43.270
Yep. The barbecue was her idea in the first place.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.970
Things like that are so nice.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:46.580
Huh?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:51.850
Being able to do things like that without a reason means you've got some really special friends. {## isn't this more like 'It takes a special person to do stuff like that without a reason'? Like she's lucky for having [special friends (kazoo.mov)] not for having [friends that are special to her] / ignore if I am bad at Japanese}

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.500
Say hi to all your special people for me too.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.260
Sure.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:00.500
Akane! Are you saying embarrassing things again? {## is she allowed to just cross things over like this? this must be illegal}

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:03.970
That's youth for you. {## oho, is this what we're running with now?}

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:13.360
How was helping out at Amanchu House today?

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:16.190
Well... it was pretty slow.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:20.780
But I had fun. Your grandma taught me tai chi.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:26.520
I wonder if I should just come out and say it.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.360
Huh? Say what?

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:30.390
Okay, I'll do it.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:37.340
Listen, when you first said you didn't want to come diving with us today, it kind of gave me a shock.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.620
A shock?

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:44.650
Yeah, I thought maybe I'd been running ahead on my own without considering your feelings at all. {## 'felt like ...' implies something different, in terms of it sort of implies that the -shock- felt like that, not that the shock was realizing that that might have been the case, blah blah blah}

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:45.770
What?

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:49.930
But I didn't expect it to be because you just wanted to help Granny.

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.740
That was part of it, but to be honest...

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:58.640
At the time, a sort of uneasiness washed over me.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.140
I'll come out and say it too.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:07.300
Okay.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:13.370
You're always introducing me to all sorts of fun things, but I wondered if that was really all right.

00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:14.150
Should I not?

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:16.840
No, I'm not saying that at all.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:22.550
I just thought that when the day came that we had to part, {## wahoo tenses}

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:25.530
I'd end up being empty inside.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:31.520
I felt like I needed to be able to find fun on my own. {## alt. 'fun things'; genericizing here so it's not just a single event, this is a perpetual ability}

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:34.640
That's amazing, Teko.

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:35.110
Huh?

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:38.890
I've never thought about anything like that before in my life. {## bakari}

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:43.490
But yeah, in the future when you're gone...

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:45.440
Yeah, no way.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.560
Huh? But, but...

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:47.990
Nope!

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:50.190
Impossible things are impossible! {## FUN THINGS DIE IF THEY EAT DOG FOOD}

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:54.480
It's impossible to consider right now.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:59.910
After all, there's still so many things I want to do and so many places I want to see with you. {## unwieldy but dropping 'want' is too strong I think / 'after all' enables 'so' later}

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:02.050
So I can't even think about that now. {## does not say 'muri'}

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.430
Right. {## three words for 'n'! it's too weird}

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:18.990
But I guess if that ever did happen, I'd feel lonely.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:23.480
They say the more fun something is, 
the sadder it is to see it end.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:30.870
Then let's have so much fun 
that it blows the sadness away!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.750
Huh?

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:36.350
As long as we keep on having fun, 
we'll find even more fun things to do. {## or: 'As long as we keep finding fun things, they'll lead us to ...' the 'that' in the original isn't properly attached and there's subject confusion resultantly}

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.640
So basically, um... {## basically, it's a fun-based Ponzi scheme. keep borrowing more fun and hope you never actually have to face the consequences}

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:42.520
I see, so even if it feels sad in the moment...

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:46.450
Fun is endless! {## Fun is a federal crime}

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:52.890
So you see? You're not empty at all, Teko.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:55.510
Yeah, you're right.

00:20:55.510 --> 00:21:01.330
My heart is filled up with my love for you and our fun memories together. {## parallel structure: [possessive] [noun]}

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:08.600
I love you too, Teko.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:09.330
Stop!

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:13.790
Let's head back.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:14.780
Sure.

00:21:14.780 --> 00:21:20.270
Oh, yeah! If you're a pro at finding fun, then I'll aim to become an expert!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.520
A wonderful proclamation!

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:25.430
That's Big Summer Event number eleven!

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:27.580
What? But what about the barbecue?

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:29.420
That one was normal-sized.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:30.010
Eh?!

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:37.500
No matter what awaits us in the future or how much time passes,

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:41.880
the year I met Teko will remain a special year to me forever and ever.

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:51.420
So for now, let's make this summer a special one to remember, Teko!

